  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-008">The fix is route registration + endpoint filters. Do NOT add per-handler checks — that is precisely the shape `SpeAdminTenantScopeFilter`'s doc comment argues against, and it is how this file drifted in the first place.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Prefer moving the registration onto the existing `/api/spe` group over re-attaching the two filters at nine call sites. Nine attachments is nine chances to miss the tenth route.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">If the absolute-path style genuinely blocks group registration, say so with evidence and attach BOTH filters — never just the role filter. The tenant scope is the half that stops cross-customer reach.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-003">Unresolvable `configId`, or one outside the caller's scope, is refused. Match the existing 404-not-403 convention (`SpeAdminTenantScopeFilter.cs:43-45`) — "exists but not yours" confirms another customer exists.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Inventory the SPE Admin client's callers before tightening. A refusal that breaks the admin app gets reverted, and the revert reopens all nine routes.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Add these routes to `RouteAuthorizationGuardTests`' census as part of the fix. The census missing this file is the reason the hole survived four recounts; closing the hole without closing the census leaves the next one just as invisible.</constraint>
    <constraint source="build-plan">Do not solve any part of this by granting SPE container permissions. `GrantMembershipAsync` stays at zero callers.</constraint>
  </constraints>

